Z||000006||dcaprio||12-05-2001||08:01 AM||||I just started my car after 2 weeks of sitting. I just needed to move it so I could put a cover on it for the winter. When I was sitting in the car backing it up Mighty Mouse jumped on my leg and then ran up my leg and hid behind the drivers seat. Now I'm 6 ft 250lbs but you can't believe how fast I jumped out of that car. I ran right out for the mouse traps. Anouther way to remove them with out killing them is to stat the car an put the heat on full bore and after about a hour crack the door and they will leave.||||reg||1
Z||000007||thomas_l||12-05-2001||08:55 AM||||I've never had any luck with peanut butter on mouse traps. The little bastards lick the pb off the trap without tripping the latch  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">. I use some stringy meat like chicken and push it thru the clip so they have to tug on their last meal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||10
